search_logs.log:
Search date: 30–31 Oct 2026.

SOURCES
- ICORE2026 ranks were read directly from portal.core.edu.au (curl):
  - acronym queries;
  - title keyword queries (Learning, Machine, Evolutionary, Genetic, Swarm, Uncertain, Causal, Knowledge, Optimi, Neural, Artificial Intelligence, Data Mining, Australasian);
  - the full FoR 4611 (Machine Learning) listing.

- The PMLR index was used to check which candidates actually publish proceedings there.
- Official sites were fetched for: ALT, CLeaR (read from its JS bundle), CPAL, PPSN, EvoStar 2027, CPAIOR 2027, SAT 2027, ICDE 2027, PRICAI 2026, BRACIS 2026, IJCLR 2026, NeSy 2026, PGM 2026, COPA, NLDL, ANTS 2026, SoCS 2026, EMO 2027 and the SIGEVO FOGA page.

LIMITATIONS
 Later facts come only from fetching known official URLs.
- Google Scholar h5 metrics and acceptance rates were not collected; the only rate obtained is BRACIS (2026 acceptance figures).
- Facts reported only by aggregators:
  - SIAM MDS26 dates (siam.org was blocked by Cloudflare);
  - IEEE CEC 2027 dates (no official site found);
  - CPAIOR 2027 deadlines;
  - the EMO 2027 deadline.

CHECKED AND NOT PROPOSED
- Inactive or unverified:
  - MSML: last PMLR volume is 2022; appears inactive.
  - ICGI: last PMLR volume is 2023; current status unverified.
  - ACM-IMS FODS: no recent edition found.
  - LION: absent from ICORE2026; not verified.
  - BayesComp and ISBA meetings: not verified before the budget ran out.
  - AJCAI (Australasian B): the ajcai2026.org domain has expired and is for sale.
  - NeuS (Neuro-symbolic Systems, PMLR 2025): too new and unverified.
- Not independent submission venues:
  - EurIPS: a NeurIPS-endorsed satellite that presents NeurIPS papers.
  - WCCI: an umbrella event; IJCNN is already tracked and CEC is proposed instead.
- Too broad, lower-tier, or tied to a SciTePress series:
  - ICPRAM (C, SciTePress, closer to signals-vision);
  - ICAART (B, SciTePress, broad);
  - IJCCI and DATA (C, SciTePress);
  - ICTAI (B, very broad);
  - KSEM, CD-MAKE, IPMU and ECSQARU (C);
  - ISIPTA (PMLR, biennial, niche imprecise probability; a possible later low-priority addition);
  - DaWaK and ASONAM (B, but lower-tier community standing);
  - ISNN, IEEE SIS and EvoMUSART;
  - EvoLearn (new EvoStar track in 2027).
- Database flagships VLDB, SIGMOD, EDBT and DASFAA are database systems rather than ML; ICDE is offered as their single representative.
- Logic-heavy KR venues (LPNMR, JELIA, ICLP, COMMA, TARK, ICCBR) were left for possible review under KR scope.
- RLC belongs to the rl-control family.
- Previously deferred CADE, IJCAR, RuleML+RR, DAI and ICWM were not re-proposed: no new evidence.
- No federated-learning-specific standalone venue of adequate standing was found; the topic is covered by NeurIPS, ICML and MLSys.

EXCLUDED AS PREDATORY OR LOW QUALITY
- MLDM (ibai-publishing);
- HIS and SoCPaR (MIR Labs);
- WASET-style ICML*/ICMLT/ICMLSC look-alikes;
- IC-AI (CSREA/WORLDCOMP, national USA);
- ICMLC (national China);
- DCAI and HAIS (national Spain);
- IEEE CAI: not a predatory series, but excluded because ieeecai.org now redirects to a gambling site, so no trustworthy official URL could be confirmed.

IDENTITY NOTES
- ANTS here is Swarm Intelligence, not the Algorithmic Number Theory Symposium.
- The tracked SIAM DS is Applications of Dynamical Systems; SIAM MDS is a different meeting.
- EvoApplications and EvoCOP share the EvoStar event and deadlines with the tracked EuroGP.
